ascendingRuns -- computes the ascending runs of a permutation
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ascendingRuns w
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * Outputs:
      * allRuns, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

An ascending run is a maximal subsequence of successive ascents.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}  |
|                                  |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4}   |
|                                  |
|o1 : Permutation                  |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : ascendingRuns p              |
|                                  |
|o2 = {1 : (3), (1, 2, 5), 1 : (4)}|
|                                  |
|o2 : List                         |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ascents: ascents, -- computes the ascents of a permutation
  * *note descendingRuns: descendingRuns, -- computes the descending runs of a
    permutation
  * *note descents: descents, -- computes the descents of a permutation
  * *note exceedances: exceedances, -- computes the exceedances of a
    permutation
  * *note saliances: saliances, -- computes the saliances of a permutation
  * *note records: records, -- computes the saliances of a permutation

Ways to use ascendingRuns:
==========================

  * "ascendingRuns(Permutation)"

