ascents -- computes the ascents of a permutation
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ascents w
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

A permutation $p=(p_1 \, \dots \, p_n)$ has an ascent at $i$ (for $i < n$) if
$p(i) < p(i+1)$.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : ascents p                  |
|                                |
|o2 = {2, 3}                     |
|                                |
|o2 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ascendingRuns: ascendingRuns, -- computes the ascending runs of a
    permutation
  * *note descendingRuns: descendingRuns, -- computes the descending runs of a
    permutation
  * *note descents: descents, -- computes the descents of a permutation
  * *note exceedances: exceedances, -- computes the exceedances of a
    permutation
  * *note saliances: saliances, -- computes the saliances of a permutation
  * *note records: records, -- computes the saliances of a permutation

Ways to use ascents:
====================

  * "ascents(Permutation)"

