avoidsPattern -- whether a permutation avoids a pattern
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        avoidsPattern(w, pattern)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * pattern, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * isAvoiding, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Pattern avoidance is more easily understood through an example. A permutation
$p$ is $2143$-avoiding if there do not exist indices $i < j < k < l$ such that
$w_j < w_i < w_l < w_k$.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : avoidsPattern(p, {2,1,4,3})|
|                                |
|o2 = false                      |
+--------------------------------+

Acknowledgement
