Bruhat order -- an overview of the Bruhat order for permutations
****************************************************************

The (strong) Bruhat order is a partial order on the symmetric group
$\mathfrak{S}_n$. See [BB05] for more details on Bruhat order.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,5,1,2,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 5, 1, 2, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : q = permutation {4,5,1,2,3}|
|                                |
|o2 = Permutation{4, 5, 1, 2, 3} |
|                                |
|o2 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : strongBruhatOrder(p, q)    |
|                                |
|o3 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+

The (right) weak Bruhat order is a partial order on the symmetric group
$\mathfrak{S}_n$. For two permutations $p$ and $q$, $w \leq_R v$ if and only if
$\ell(w) + \ell(v^{-1} w) = \ell(v)$, where $\ell$ denotes the *note
length(Permutation): length_lpPermutation_rp, of a permutation and $\leq_R$ is
the right weak Bruhat order.

+----------------------------+
|i4 : p = permutation {1,3,2}|
|                            |
|o4 = Permutation{1, 3, 2}   |
|                            |
|o4 : Permutation            |
+----------------------------+
|i5 : q = permutation {3,1,2}|
|                            |
|o5 = Permutation{3, 1, 2}   |
|                            |
|o5 : Permutation            |
+----------------------------+
|i6 : weakBruhatOrder(p, q)  |
|                            |
|o6 = true                   |
+----------------------------+

The optional argument *note Side: weakBruhatOrder, can be used to specify which
weak Bruhat order to use. The current options are "left" and "right" (default).

+----------------------------------------+
|i7 : weakBruhatOrder(p, q, Side=>"left")|
|                                        |
|o7 = false                              |
+----------------------------------------+

We can use these orders to construct the poset of $\mathfrak{S}_n$ using the
*note Posets: (Posets)Top, package. The *note symmetricGroupPoset:
symmetricGroupPoset, method constructs the poset of $\mathfrak{S}_n$ with the
Bruhat order for convenience.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : P = symmetricGroupPoset(4, strongBruhatOrder)|
|                                                  |
|o8 = P                                            |
|                                                  |
|o8 : Poset                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Q = symmetricGroupPoset(4, weakBruhatOrder)  |
|                                                  |
|o9 = Q                                            |
|                                                  |
|o9 : Poset                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------+

This allows us to verify, for example, that the weak Bruhat order is
rank-symmetric and Sperner [GG20].

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : rankPoly = rankGeneratingFunction Q                                    |
|                                                                             |
|       6     5     4     3     2                                             |
|o10 = q  + 3q  + 5q  + 6q  + 5q  + 3q + 1                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : ZZ[q]                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : coeffs = apply(flatten entries (coefficients rankPoly)#1, k -> sub(k,  |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = {1, 3, 5, 6, 5, 3, 1}                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : List                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|ZZ))                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : d = (degree rankPoly)#0                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = 6                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : all(apply(#coeffs // 2, i -> coeffs#i == coeffs#(d-i)))                |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = true                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : isSperner P                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o14 = true                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

  * [BB05] Anders Björner and Francesco Brenti, Combinatorics of Coxeter groups
    (see https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/3-540-27596-7 ), Graduate Texts
    in Mathematics, 231, Springer, New York, 2005
  * [GG20] Christian Gaetz and Yibo Gao, The weak Bruhat order on the symmetric
    group is Sperner, Sém. Lothar. Combin. 82B (2020), Art. 35, 8 pp.
