cycleDecomposition -- computes the decomposition of a permutation as a product of disjoint cycles
*************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        cycleDecomposition w
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Every permutation can be decomposed into a product of disjoint cycles. We
follow the convention to write the decomposition in its "canonical" or
"standard" form. So

1. each cycle is listed with its largest element first, and 
 2. the cycles are listed in increasing order.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : cycleDecomposition p       |
|                                |
|o2 = {(3, 2, 1), (5, 4)}        |
|                                |
|o2 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cycleType: cycleType, -- computes the cycle type of a permutation

Ways to use cycleDecomposition:
===============================

  * "cycleDecomposition(Permutation)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note cycleDecomposition: cycleDecomposition, is a *note method
function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

