exceedances -- computes the exceedances of a permutation
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        exceedances w
        exceedances(w, Weak)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Weak => ..., default value false
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

A permutation $p=(p_1 \, \dots \, p_n)$ has an exceedance at $i$ if $p(i) > i$.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : exceedances p              |
|                                |
|o2 = {1, 4}                     |
|                                |
|o2 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+

This is called a weak exceedance if the inequality is not strict, i.e., $p(i)
\geq i$.

+--------------------------------+
|i3 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o3 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o3 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : exceedances(p, Weak=>true) |
|                                |
|o4 = {1, 4}                     |
|                                |
|o4 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+

