extend(Permutation,Permutation) -- rewrites two permutations to be permutations on the same number of symbols
*************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note extend: (Macaulay2Doc)extend,
  * Usage: 
        e = extend(w,v)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * v, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Verify (missing documentation) => ..., default value true, 
  * Outputs:
      * e, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, 

Description
===========

For ease, we can also extend two permutations so that they are regarded as
permutations on the same number of symbols. More precisely, if we have
permutations $p=(p_1, \dots, p_n)$ and $q=(q_1, \dots, q_m)$, then extend(p,q)
will return both $p$ and $q$ as permutations on $\text{max}(m,n)$ symbols.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}                                         |
|                                                                         |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4}                                          |
|                                                                         |
|o1 : Permutation                                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : q = permutation {2,3,1,4,5,7,6}                                     |
|                                                                         |
|o2 = Permutation{2, 3, 1, 4, 5, 7, 6}                                    |
|                                                                         |
|o2 : Permutation                                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : extend(p,q)                                                         |
|                                                                         |
|o3 = (Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4, 6, 7}, Permutation{2, 3, 1, 4, 5, 7, 6})|
|                                                                         |
|o3 : Sequence                                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note extend(Permutation,ZZ): extend, -- rewrites a permutation as a
    permutation on more symbols
  * *note trim: (Macaulay2Doc)trim, -- minimize generators and relations

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note extend(Permutation,Permutation):
    extend_lpPermutation_cmPermutation_rp, -- rewrites two permutations to be
    permutations on the same number of symbols
