Permutation -- the Permutation type
***********************************

Description
===========

Permutations are constructed from lists. To create a permutation, use the
permutation method.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,4,5}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 4, 5} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+

Permutations must be constructed from lists consisting of only the integers $1
\dots n$. If a list contains any other elements or does not consist of the
entire range, then an error is thrown.

Functions and methods returning a permutation:
==============================================

  * "extend(Permutation,ZZ)" -- see *note extend: extend, -- rewrites a
    permutation as a permutation on more symbols
  * "foataBijection(Permutation)" -- see *note foataBijection: foataBijection,
    -- computes the image of a permutation under the Foata bijection
  * *note inverse(Permutation): inverse_lpPermutation_rp, -- computes the
    inverse of a permutation
  * "permutation(VisibleList)"
  * *note Permutation * Permutation: Permutation _st Permutation, -- computes
    the product of two permutations
  * *note Permutation ^ ZZ: Permutation ^ ZZ, -- computes the power of a
    permutation
  * "randomPermutation(ZZ)" -- see *note randomPermutation: randomPermutation,
    -- generates a random permutation
  * "transposition(ZZ)" -- see *note transposition: transposition, --
    constructs a transposition
  * "transposition(ZZ,ZZ)" -- see *note transposition: transposition, --
    constructs a transposition
  * "trim(Permutation)" -- see *note trim: trim, -- rewrites a permutation in
    its smallest representation

