Permutations/Documentation/operationsDocs.m2:339:0.

File: Permutations.info, Node: Permutation _st VisibleList, Next: Permutation == Permutation, Prev: Permutation _st Permutation, Up: Top

Permutation * VisibleList -- computes the action of a permutation on a list
***************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        w * l
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * l, a *note visible list: (Macaulay2Doc)VisibleList,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note visible list: (Macaulay2Doc)VisibleList,, 

Description
===========

A permutation $p$ acts on the elements of list by permuting the elements of the
list according to the permutation. More precisely, if $L = \{ e_1, \dots, e_k
\}$ is a list and $p=(p_1, \dots, p_n)$ is a permutation, then the action is
given by $p*L = \{ e_{p(1)}, \dots, e_{p(k)}}$.

The permutation cannot permute more than #l elements.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4,7,6} |
|                                     |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4, 7, 6}|
|                                     |
|o1 : Permutation                     |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = {3,1,2,5,4,6,7}             |
|                                     |
|o2 = {3, 1, 2, 5, 4, 6, 7}           |
|                                     |
|o2 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : p * L                           |
|                                     |
|o3 = {2, 3, 1, 4, 5, 7, 6}           |
|                                     |
|o3 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+

The permutation can be a permutation on less than #l elements.

+--------------------------------+
|i4 : p = permutation {3,1,2,4,5}|
|                                |
|o4 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 4, 5} |
|                                |
|o4 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : L = {3,1,2,5,4,6,7}        |
|                                |
|o5 = {3, 1, 2, 5, 4, 6, 7}      |
|                                |
|o5 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : p * L                      |
|                                |
|o6 = {2, 3, 1, 5, 4, 6, 7}      |
|                                |
|o6 : List                       |
+--------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note VisibleList _ Permutation: VisibleList _us Permutation, -- computes
    the action of a permutation on a list

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Permutation * VisibleList: Permutation _st VisibleList, -- computes
    the action of a permutation on a list
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

