Permutation ^ ZZ -- computes the power of a permutation
*******************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        w^n
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note permutation: Permutation,, 

Description
===========

Computes the power of a permutation. The power can be any integer.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : p^2                        |
|                                |
|o2 = Permutation{2, 3, 1}       |
|                                |
|o2 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : p^0                        |
|                                |
|o3 = Permutation{1, 2, 3, 4, 5} |
|                                |
|o3 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : p^(-3)                     |
|                                |
|o4 = Permutation{1, 2, 3, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o4 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Permutation ^ ZZ: Permutation ^ ZZ, -- computes the power of a
    permutation
