sign(Permutation) -- computes the sign of a permutation
*******************************************************

  * Function: *note sign: (Macaulay2Doc)sign,
  * Usage: 
        sign w
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

Every permutation can be written as a product of transpositions. One definition
for the sign of a permutation $p$ is $1$ if it can be written as a product of
an even number of transpositions and is $-1$ if it can be written as an odd
number of transpositions.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,1,2,5,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 1, 2, 5, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : sign p                     |
|                                |
|o2 = -1                         |
+--------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cycleDecomposition: cycleDecomposition, -- computes the decomposition
    of a permutation as a product of disjoint cycles
  * *note cycleType: cycleType, -- computes the cycle type of a permutation
  * *note isEven: isEven, -- whether a permutation is even
  * *note isOdd: isOdd, -- whether a permutation is odd

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note sign(Permutation): sign_lpPermutation_rp, -- computes the sign of a
    permutation
