strongBruhatOrder -- compares two permutations in the (strong) Bruhat order
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        strongBruhatOrder(w,v)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * v, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

The (strong) Bruhat order is a partial order on the symmetric group
$\mathfrak{S}_n$. See [BB05] for more details on the strong Bruhat order.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {3,5,1,2,4}|
|                                |
|o1 = Permutation{3, 5, 1, 2, 4} |
|                                |
|o1 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : q = permutation {4,5,1,2,3}|
|                                |
|o2 = Permutation{4, 5, 1, 2, 3} |
|                                |
|o2 : Permutation                |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : strongBruhatOrder(p, q)    |
|                                |
|o3 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+

References
==========

  * [BB05] Anders Björner and Francesco Brenti, Combinatorics of Coxeter groups
    (see https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/3-540-27596-7 ), Graduate Texts
    in Mathematics, 231, Springer, New York, 2005

