weakBruhatOrder -- compares two permutations in the weak Bruhat order
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        weakBruhatOrder(w,v)
  * Inputs:
      * w, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * v, a *note permutation: Permutation,, 
      * Side, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, an optional argument to
        specify the side of the Bruhat order
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Side => ..., default value "right"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

The (right) weak Bruhat order is a partial order on the symmetric group
$\mathfrak{S}_n$. For two permutations $p$ and $q$, $w \leq_R v$ if and only if
$\ell(w) + \ell(v^{-1} w) = \ell(v)$, where $\ell$ denotes the *note
length(Permutation): length_lpPermutation_rp, of a permutation and $\leq_R$ is
the right weak Bruhat order. See [BB05] for more details on the weak Bruhat
order.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : p = permutation {1,3,2}|
|                            |
|o1 = Permutation{1, 3, 2}   |
|                            |
|o1 : Permutation            |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : q = permutation {2,1,3}|
|                            |
|o2 = Permutation{2, 1, 3}   |
|                            |
|o2 : Permutation            |
+----------------------------+
|i3 : r = permutation {3,1,2}|
|                            |
|o3 = Permutation{3, 1, 2}   |
|                            |
|o3 : Permutation            |
+----------------------------+
|i4 : weakBruhatOrder(p, r)  |
|                            |
|o4 = true                   |
+----------------------------+
|i5 : weakBruhatOrder(q, r)  |
|                            |
|o5 = false                  |
+----------------------------+

By default, weakBruhatOrder computes the right weak Bruhat order, but the
optional argument {tt Side} can be used to compute, for example, the left weak
Bruhat order. The current options for Side are "left" and "right".

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : p = permutation {1,3,2}                            |
|                                                        |
|o6 = Permutation{1, 3, 2}                               |
|                                                        |
|o6 : Permutation                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : r = permutation {3,1,2}                            |
|                                                        |
|o7 = Permutation{3, 1, 2}                               |
|                                                        |
|o7 : Permutation                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : weakBruhatOrder(inverse p, inverse r, Side=>"left")|
|                                                        |
|o8 = true                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

References
==========

  * [BB05] Anders Björner and Francesco Brenti, Combinatorics of Coxeter groups
    (see https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/3-540-27596-7 ), Graduate Texts
    in Mathematics, 231, Springer, New York, 2005

See also
========

  * *note length(Permutation): length_lpPermutation_rp, -- computes the length
    of a permutation
  * *note strongBruhatOrder: strongBruhatOrder, -- compares two permutations in
    the (strong) Bruhat order
  * *note symmetricGroupPoset: symmetricGroupPoset, -- constructs the poset of
    the symmetric group under a partial order

Ways to use weakBruhatOrder:
============================

  * "weakBruhatOrder(Permutation,Permutation)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note weakBruhatOrder: weakBruhatOrder, is a *note method function
with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

